Dear Hiring Team,

I am excited to apply for the *Software Engineer* role with GitHub's Security Products team. I bring more than three years of professional software engineering experience and a Master of Science in Computer Science from Pace University. Most recently, I automated daily code-review triage across 25–30 pull requests per week, saving reviewers several hours of manual work and helping them focus on higher-value decisions.

At Sperse, I created a React Flow and TypeScript platform that lets customers build and monitor agentic workflows, with Temporal providing reliable, resumable execution. I also built a secure Python and FastAPI CRM platform serving 10,000+ users, a monitored API layer exposing 160+ backend actions, and GitHub Actions pipelines that flag latency, accuracy, and safety issues before production. Earlier at Qualitest, I built a Java and Spring Boot storage service, improved PostgreSQL performance, delivered React visualizations, and strengthened recovery across 100K+ weekly AWS Step Functions executions.

GitHub's mission to build the home for all developers—and the Security Products team's focus on preventing credential leaks—connects directly with my completed Granular Guard project. Its Go API separates Git diffs into reviewable sections, detects credentials in added lines, and isolates risky sections while safe work continues. The JavaScript interface provides masked guidance and server-validated approvals, while automated tests, GitHub Actions CI, structured logs, health checks, and Docker support reliable delivery. This reflects how I approach security: protect customers while keeping the developer experience clear and productive.

I am drawn to GitHub's customer-obsessed, ship-to-learn, and own-the-outcome principles. I would welcome the opportunity to bring my experience with Go, JavaScript, APIs, automated testing, CI/CD, and user-facing software to a distributed team securing the world's software. I can be reached at #ph or #eml. Thank you for your time and consideration, I look forward to connecting!

